From: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 00:29:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: wsa884x: complete SP11 DP1/DP3 SIMPLE transport fields

After the DP2/COMP OffsetCtrl2=0x07 correction in patch 0065, two known
Windows slave-transport fields remain absent from the SP11 WSA8845 SIMPLE
port declarations.  qcaucd programs DP1/DAC BlockCtrl3=0x00 and
DP3/BOOST OffsetCtrl2=0x1f on both amplifiers.

The SoundWire core already derives both values from the Qualcomm master
schedule and patch 0065 already provides optional SIMPLE register support.
Advertise BlockCtrl3 for DP1/DAC and OffsetCtrl2 for DP3/BOOST.  No constant
register value, gain, PA state, lifecycle policy or DSP calibration changes.

This patch is incremental on top of 0065 and is structural parity work; it
is not part of the causal DP2 broadband-static fix.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <codex@openai.com>
---
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wsa884x.c
@@ -860,6 +860,7 @@
 		.max_ch = 1,
 		.simple_ch_prep_sm = true,
 		.read_only_wordlength = true,
+		.simple_transport_registers = SDW_DPN_SIMPLE_TRANSPORT_BLOCKCTRL3,
 	},
 	[WSA884X_PORT_COMP] = {
 		.num = WSA884X_PORT_COMP + 1,
@@ -877,6 +878,7 @@
 		.max_ch = 1,
 		.simple_ch_prep_sm = true,
 		.read_only_wordlength = true,
+		.simple_transport_registers = SDW_DPN_SIMPLE_TRANSPORT_OFFSETCTRL2,
 	},
 	[WSA884X_PORT_PBR] = {
 		.num = WSA884X_PORT_PBR + 1,
